  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_036 (SCVI n200, ViT-L, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 acc, showing that the RNA encoder choice is the dominant factor (SCVI >> PCA >> scGPT). However, we only have one data point on aggregation for SCVI (avgpool). For PCA, avgpool outperformed transformer by ~3% (0.629 vs 0.599), but it is unclear whether this ordering holds for the richer SCVI latent representations, which may interact differently with attention-based aggregation. config_038 (SCVI n200, ViT-L, transformer, concat) directly tests this: if transformer is worse or equal, we can confidently lock in avgpool and spend remaining budget on other axes (fusion, image encoder); if transformer is meaningfully better, it reveals that SCVI's structured latent space benefits from attention-based profile integration, opening a new optimization direction. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a key design uncertainty around the current best configuration without changing multiple variables simultaneously."
